@Chri.z I do agree with @ROME|King Bryan-Titan Analytics that right now it's more of an intra-faction competition vs. if the entire pool was up for grabs, we would have a stronger faction vs. faction or guild vs. guild dynamics.

I do understand the original thinking around creating faction balance, but if there is intra-faction friendly fire... then that whole concept doesn't matter anymore.  Galia will become a free for all.

#FreeGalia

⁠archived-foundation-room⁠

@Kr1gs I hear what you are saying about a potential map reset being discouraging. The "meaningful progress" that comes from playing starbased is the Atlas earnings from the LP exchange (and selling  materials found in game to those players on the galactic marketplace) and the XP gains from playing the game. 

Maybe there's some things we can do differently to minimize the impact of a map reset. Like enabling local markets. Open to suggestions.

@ROME I TONY1 
this doesn’t seem like a game of territory and conquest

It was not a game of territory and conquest before. It still is not. It will be.

__

@BRUNN Regarding ⁠archived-foundation-room⁠

Combat will be PVP combat in the initial release. PvE is coming later. It looks like with Season 1: https://portal.productboard.com/staratlas/1-star-atlas-roadmap/c/75-sage-new-pve-enemies, though some of it may come during the Pre-season already: https://portal.productboard.com/staratlas/1-star-atlas-roadmap/c/31-sage-medium-risk-zone (it's not entirely clear)
